# Security Rules

- All `/admin` routes must be protected server-side.
- Every mutation and sensitive CV access must perform server-side authorization.
- Never trust role/permission values from the browser.
- ADMIN and STAFF roles are distinct.
- Permanent deletion is ADMIN-only and archive-gated.
- Use secure server-side sessions and secure cookies in production.
- Passwords must be strongly hashed; never store plaintext passwords.
- Login must have brute-force/rate-limit protection.
- Protect against IDOR, privilege escalation, CSRF where applicable, XSS, injection, session attacks, mass assignment, and information leakage.
- Never expose WorkDrive credentials to the browser.
- CV access must be authorized and mediated server-side.
- Do not use dangerouslySetInnerHTML for untrusted content.
- Do not log passwords, tokens, CV contents, or unnecessary PII.
- Minimize PII in audit records.
